commit 91dc6b63d5cc58efda089e270a9f06197ddefcce
Author: InnoPeak <global_ai@innopeaktech.com>
Date:   Wed May 20 00:54:56 2026 -0700

    feat(grid-persistence): LayoutStore seam with whiteout-safe hydrate
    
    Why
    - G1.5 needs Grid persistence to consume the Repository v0 contract
      from G2.1, restore all open Grids on startup, and survive corrupted
      persisted state without whiteing out the desktop. The hook currently
      reads/writes localStorage synchronously, which couples the runtime to
      one backend and offers no recovery if the parsed payload is missing
      required arrays.
    
    What
    - Add `packages/plugin-organizer/src/layoutStore.ts` exporting a
      `LayoutStore` interface, `localStorageLayoutStore()` (default;
      preserves the historical sync path), and `repositoryLayoutStore()`
      backed by `GridEntity`/`GridItemEntity` repos.
    - Both adapters catch errors and surface them via optional
      `onLoadError`/`onSaveError` callbacks. Returning `null` from `load()`
      signals "no prior state" and never throws.
    - Wire `GridSystemProvider` to accept `store?: LayoutStore` (defaults
      to localStorage). Hydrate is now async with a defence-in-depth
      try/catch that falls back to empty state if any future store throws.
      `save` and `clearAll` delegate to the store.
    - Add `@repo/core-data` to plugin-organizer workspace deps so the new
      adapter can import the entity types and `createInMemoryRepo`.
    - Add 9 vitest cases in `src/layoutStore.test.ts`: round-trip, missing
      key, malformed JSON, type guard, save quota error, repo empty
      layout, repo round-trip, cull-on-disappearance, repo load failure.
    
    Scope
    - packages/plugin-organizer/ (layoutStore + provider refactor + tests
      + package.json), packages/grid-persistence/docs/, G1 manifest,
      autorun log. No Tauri or Host runtime changes; the host can opt into
      `repositoryLayoutStore` once `tauri-sqlite` adapters are wired (G3-E1
      / runtime follow-up).
    
    Risk
    - Low. Default behaviour is unchanged because the provider keeps using
      `localStorageLayoutStore()` when no `store` prop is supplied. New
      async hydrate path keeps the same eventual-state shape (empty layout
      on any error).
    
    Docs
    - packages/grid-persistence/docs/dev_log.md → READY_TO_SHIP, G1
      manifest row #5 → READY_TO_SHIP, autorun log checkpoint.
    
    Tests
    - pnpm --filter @repo/plugin-organizer test : 13 tests PASS
    - pnpm --filter @repo/plugin-organizer check-types : PASS
    - pnpm --filter desktop build : PASS
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

